From: PS5_Proton
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: Mica taskbar and live window previews

The Mihawk taskbar declares a Mica backdrop through the public DWM API and
paints with alpha: buffered paint clears to glass, GDI marks become opaque and
the clock uses composited theme text. Hovering an application button shows a
rounded acrylic pop-up with the window title and its live DWM thumbnail,
scaled to fit, or its icon while minimized; clicking it activates the window.
Wine owns the windows and the compositor draws the retained pixels; nothing
is copied. Tooltips, keyboard navigation and button semantics are unchanged.

